{
  "_comment": [
    "Regression thresholds for benchmarks/memory_profile.py, checked by",
    "benchmarks/check_memory_thresholds.py. These are limits, not measurements:",
    "they are hand-set and versioned deliberately, unlike benchmark results,",
    "which are build artefacts (see docs/benchmarking.md).",
    "",
    "max_traced_peak_mib is a tracemalloc figure, so it measures Python",
    "allocations rather than RSS and is comparable across runners. The inbound",
    "persistence scenario also has a deliberately generous GitHub Actions RSS",
    "delta gate so aggregate process growth cannot escape the logical cap.",
    "Each tracemalloc value is a reviewed bound for the current scenario. The",
    "property-heavy bound was compared against earlier candidate runs before",
    "this update; the WebSocket logical counters mirror its bounded 256 KiB",
    "coalescing implementation.",
    "",
    "logical is an exact-match assertion on the scenario's 'loaded' counters. It",
    "is machine-independent and catches a benchmark that silently stopped doing",
    "the same work, which a memory number alone would reward."
  ],
